## Face Recognition Algorithms

| Algorithm | Detection | Embedding | Speed | Accuracy | Best For |
|-----------|-----------|-----------|-------|----------|----------|
| **HOG + Dlib** | HOG | Dlib ResNet | ⚡ Fast | Good | CPU-only, real-time |
| **DeepFace** | RetinaFace | Facenet512 | 🐢 Slow | Excellent | High accuracy needs |
| **InsightFace** | Built-in | Buffalo | ⚡ Fast | Excellent | GPU acceleration |
| **MTCNN + FaceNet** | MTCNN | FaceNet | 🔄 Medium | Good | Balanced performance |

### HOG + Dlib
- Uses **Histogram of Oriented Gradients (HOG)** for face detection
- **Dlib's ResNet** model for 128-dimensional face embeddings
- Lightweight, works well on CPU without GPU
- Best for real-time applications with limited resources

### DeepFace (Facenet512 + RetinaFace)
- **RetinaFace** detector for accurate face localization
- **Facenet512** generates 512-dimensional embeddings
- Highest accuracy but slower processing
- Best when accuracy is priority over speed

### InsightFace (Buffalo)
- All-in-one face analysis framework
- **Buffalo** model for detection + recognition
- Optimized for both CPU and GPU
- Best balance of speed and accuracy

### MTCNN + FaceNet
- **Multi-task Cascaded CNN (MTCNN)** for face detection
- **FaceNet** for face embeddings
- Good accuracy with moderate speed
- Robust to various face angles

## Algorithm Selection Guide

| Scenario | Recommended Algorithm |
|----------|----------------------|
| Low-end hardware / CPU only | HOG + Dlib |
| Maximum accuracy needed | DeepFace |
| GPU available, balanced needs | InsightFace |
| Variable lighting/angles | MTCNN + FaceNet |

